<title>PERU: Peru's Edegel, Edelnor announce cash dividends.</title>
<headline>Peru's Edegel, Edelnor announce cash dividends.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peruvian electric generator Edegel and distributor Edelnor will pay cash dividends to shareholders of record as of August 5, the Lima Stock Exchange said Monday.</p>
<p>Edegel, bought in 1995 by a consortium of U.S. Entergy Corp, Chile's Endesa and Peru's Grana y Montero and Banco Wiese, will pay dividends totaling 82.6 million soles, or 0.037114 soles per share. The dividend will be paid on August 22.</p>
<p>Edelnor, which is owned by the Spanish-Chilean consortium of Endesa, Enersis and Chilectra will pay a total of 28.2 million soles, or 0.03683 soles per share on August 13.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
